rent orphan body allowed fields: `{\\\"by\\\", \\\"log_index\\\", \\\"reason\\\", \\\"statement_b64\\\"}`\\n\\nI need to add `entries_b64` to the allowed fields.\\n\\nThe predicate has: `{\\\"from_seq\\\", \\\"to_seq\\\", \\\"prev_sha256\\\", \\\"head_sha256\\\"}`\\n\\nThe entries in `entries_b64` should be the canonical entry bytes for entries `from_seq` through `to_seq`.\\n\\nLet me implement this step by step.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll implement the required function and wire it into the orphan checking logic.\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-77fc73fa-f8bb-4af0-9db2-58b42cc14061","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"oldText":"    else:  # orphan: explains a Rekor attestation by the writer that the ledger doesn't hold\n        allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\"}\n        if _need(body, \"log_index\", int, where) < 0 or not _need(body, \"reason\", str, where).strip():\n            raise Bad(f\"{where}: orphan needs log_index >= 0 and a reason\")\n        try:  # the orphaned attestation's exact signed statement; monitor checks it against Rekor's payload hash\n            base64.b64decode(_need(body, \"statement_b64\", str, where), validate=True)\n        except ValueError:\n            raise Bad(f\"{where}: statement_b64 must be base64\")","newText":"    else:  # orphan: explains a Rekor attestation by the writer that the ledger doesn't hold\n        allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\", \"entries_b64\"}\n        if _need(body, \"log_index\", int, where) < 0 or not _need(body, \"reason\", str, where).strip():\n            raise Bad(f\"{where}: orphan needs log_index >= 0 and a reason\")\n        try:  # the orphaned attestation's exact signed statement; monitor checks it against Rekor's payload hash\n            base64.b64decode(_need(body, \"statement_b64\", str, where), validate=True)\n        except ValueError:\n            raise Bad(f\"{where}: statement_b64